  "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{b}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{b}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4\\sqrt{b}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4\\sqrt{b}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{b}}{\\sqrt{b}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b})\\sqrt{b}}{4(\\sqrt{b})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{a}\\cdot \\sqrt{b}-(\\sqrt{b})^{2}}{4(\\sqrt{b})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{ab}-b}{4b}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
